        "original_id": "3c5c6da0-1996-5ff7-8e3d-6a2df69faebe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Magazines: Antic, The Chronicle of Philanthropy\n- Products: Atari 8-bit family, Atari 400/800, XL, XE, XEGS\n- People: Phil Semas, Stacy Palmer\n- Topics: home computing, nonprofit world\n\nFacts:\n- Antic was a home computer magazine devoted to the Atari 8-bit family, including the Atari 400/800, XL, XE, and XEGS.\n- Antic was published from April 1982 until June/July 1990.\n- The Chronicle of Philanthropy was founded in 1988 by editor Phil Semas and then managing editor Stacy Palmer.\n- The Chronicle of Philanthropy is a magazine that covers the nonprofit world.",
